# The root R0 without an entry. The actuals are obtained by execution: `Pick\PickArgs()` is an ordinary Structure whose
# data describes a reference result (`return: @` in Pick); it counts its run and returns the Structure Args (a 7).
# The code operand was read first, as written. The call then executes Host\add over Host with the fields of Args
# supplied: Log\made 1, Log\seen 7, and the statement after the call is reached (Log\after 1).
# Norm: the book #structural-call (the operands are evaluated in the order they are written; `call(args code)` is one
# call; «exactly the argument Structure of an ordinary call»), #return-in-data.
@: Log (int: made 0; int: seen 0; int: after 0)
@: Host (int: a 1; return: int; add(Log\seen := a; return: a))
@: Pick (return: @; Args(int: a 7); PickCode(Log\made := Log\made + 1; return: Host\add); PickArgs(Log\made := Log\made + 1; return: node\Args))
call(code := Host\add; args := Pick\PickArgs())
Log\after := 1
